  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Michigan received $127M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Total award count in the state is 8,972 and average award size is $14.2K. Obligations are down 98.7% year over year. Historic obligations show a sharp drop from prior full fiscal years: FY22 had $12.9B, FY23 had $12B, FY24 had $11B, FY25 had $8.9B, and FY26 had $9.4B, compared with $127M so far in FY27. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer in the state in FY2027 to date with $76M, followed by the General Services Administration with $33.8M and the Department of Justice with $5.9M. Daniels Building Co Inc leads vendors with $23.4M, followed by FORD MOTOR CO with $12.2M and TRILLAMED LLC with $11M. Automobile Manufacturing is the largest industry category in FY2027 to date with $24.6M, followed by Electrical Contractors and Other Wiring Installation Contractors with $23.7M and Engineering Services with $14.5M. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed in FY2027 to date compared with prior years?",
        "body": "Obligations in FY2027 to date are $127M, down 98.7% year over year. Full prior fiscal years show much larger totals: FY22 had $12.9B, FY23 had $12B, FY24 had $11B, FY25 had $8.9B, and FY26 had $9.4B. The current FY27 figure is a fiscal year to date total and is partial."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest buyers and vendors in Michigan this fiscal year to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $76M, the General Services Administration obligated $33.8M, and the Department of Justice obligated $5.9M in FY2027 to date. DANIELS BUILDING CO INC received $23.4M, FORD MOTOR CO received $12.2M, and TRILLAMED LLC received $11M in the same period."
      }
    ]
  },
